<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.tThese financial results have been prepared in accordance with Indian Accounting Standards (Ind-AS) as prescribed under section 133 of Companies Act, 2013 read with Rule 3 of the companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules 2015 and relevant amendment thereafter.  n  n2.tThe Company has adopted Ind AS 116  Leases  effective April 1, 2019 and applied the standard to its Leases using the modified retrospective approach. On transition, the adoption of new standard resulted in recognition of Right-of-Use asset of Rs. 3297.34 lakhs and an equal amount of lease liability. The effect of this adoption is not material on profit and earnings per share for the quarter.  n  n3.tDuring the quarter the company has invested Rs.2700 Lakhs to acquire remaining 50% shareholding (No. of shares 7500000 ) in its Joint Venture  Company  Padget Electronics Private Limited . Consequent to this Padget Electronic Private Limited  has become wholly owned subsidiary of the Company. hence, Figures for quarter Ending June 30.2019 is not comparable with quarter  ending June  2019  &amp; March 2019  n  n4.tThe Company had made an Initial Public Offer ('IPO') during the Quarter ended 30 September, 2017, for 33,93,425 equity shares of Rs. 10 each, comprising of 3,39,750 fresh issue of equity shares by the Company and 30,53,675 equity shares offered for sale by share holders. The equity shares were issued at a price of Rs. 1,766 per share (including premium of Rs. 1,756 per share). Out of the total proceeds from the IPO of Rs. 59,928 Lakhs, the Company's share was Rs. 6,000 Lakhs from the fresh issue of 339,750 equity shares. Fresh equity shares were allotted by the Company on 14 September, 2017 and the shares of the Company were listed on the stock exchanges on 18 September, 2017.  nDetails of utilisation of IPO Proceeds are as follow  nParticularstObject of the Issue as per ProspectustTotal Utilization Up to June 30, 2019tAmount Pending Utilization  na.tRe-payment/pre-payment, in full or in part, of certain borrowings availed by the  Companyt               2,200 t               2,200 t                -     nb.tSetting up a unit for manufacturing of LED TVs at the Tirupati (A.P)t                  758 t                  549 t               209   nc.dtFinance the enhancement of our backward integration capabilities in the lighting products vertical at  Dehradun Facilityt                  886 t                  404 t               482   nd.tUpgradation of the information technology infrastructure of the Companyt               1,063 t                  653 t               410   ne.tGeneral corporate purposes (see note 'b' below)t                  805 t                  805 t                -     n tSub-totalt                  5,712 t                  4,612 t              1,100   nf.tIPO Expenses (see note 'b' below)t                  288 t                  288 t                -     n tTotalt                  6,000 t t   n  nNotes:  na.tThe company has deposited Rs. 1100 Lakhs in schedule banks  as Fixed deposit  nb.tEstimated IPO expenses reduced by Rs. 54 Lakhs and accordingly expense transferred to General Corporate Expenses.  n5.tThe above results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors in their respective meetings held on August 13, 2019. The Limited Review for the quarter ended 30 June, 2019, has been carried out by the Statutory Auditor, as required under Regulation 33 of SEBI (LODR) Regulation, 2015.  n6.tFigures of the previous periods have been regrouped /rearranged, wherever necessary  n</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
